---
import ContentPageLayout from '../layouts/ContentPageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/constants';
---
<ContentPageLayout
  title="About MiniAdda"
  description="MiniAdda is a fast crypto tool and news site: a USD converter, live prices, a Sigcamp directory and short, sourced crypto news."
  heading="About MiniAdda"
  crumb="About"
>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} is a fast, focused crypto site. Instead of long, padded articles, we give you a
    working tool first — a live crypto-to-USD converter — then clear, sourced news and answers.
  </p>
  <p>
    We cover what people actually search for: live Bitcoin and altcoin prices, how much a coin is
    worth in USD, active BitcoinTalk signature campaigns, and the day's crypto news across
    markets, technology, regulation and finance.
  </p>

  <h2>What's here</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/">Converter</a> — convert any listed coin to USD and back, instantly.</li>
    <li><a href="/prices">Prices</a> — live USD prices for every coin we track.</li>
    <li><a href="/sigcamp">Sigcamp</a> — a table of BitcoinTalk signature campaigns.</li>
    <li><a href="/news">News</a> &amp; <a href="/article">Articles</a> — short, sourced stories.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <p>
    Prices are fetched from public market data and refreshed regularly. Every story is reviewed by
    an editor before it is published; we state what is known, mark what is uncertain, and link the
    sources we used.
  </p>

  <h2>What we don't do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We don't invent authors, quotes, reviews or citations.</li>
    <li>We don't publish unverified claims as fact.</li>
    <li>We don't give financial advice. Prices are informational only.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Read our <a href="/editorial">Editorial Policy</a> for the full standard, or
    <a href="/contact">contact us</a> with a correction.
  </p>
</ContentPageLayout>
